From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Don't hint an unknown cursor position to a locked pointer.

A game that clips the cursor right after creating its window gets its
pointer locked before the first wl_pointer.enter. Wine's cursor position
is still (0,0) then, and ClipCursor sent that as the locked pointer's
position hint. The enter that followed was not hinted again, so when the
lock ended, the compositor moved the pointer to the window's top left
corner. Seen in Balatro on KWin.

Only send the hint when the pointer is on the window, or when the
application set a position with SetCursorPos.

Fixes: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/957
---
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
@@ -1398,6 +1398,7 @@
     struct wayland_win_data *data;
     RECT confine_rect;
     POINT cursor_pos, warp;
+    BOOL known_pos;
 
     TRACE("clip=%s reset=%d\n", wine_dbgstr_rect(clip), reset);
 
@@ -1407,6 +1408,11 @@
     /* the cursor pos may have changed between SetCursorPos and ClipCursor calls */
     pthread_mutex_lock(&pointer->mutex);
     if (pointer->pending_warp) cursor_pos = pointer->warp;
+    /* Before the pointer has entered the window, Wine's cursor position is
+     * not where the host pointer is. A hint from it would make the compositor
+     * move the pointer there when the lock ends, so only send one when the
+     * pointer is on the window or the application asked for a position. */
+    known_pos = pointer->pending_warp || pointer->focused_hwnd == hwnd;
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&pointer->mutex);
 
     if (!(data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd))) return FALSE;
@@ -1427,7 +1433,7 @@
         pointer->pending_warp = FALSE;
     }
 
-    if (wl_surface && hwnd == pointer->constraint_hwnd && pointer->zwp_locked_pointer_v1)
+    if (wl_surface && known_pos && hwnd == pointer->constraint_hwnd && pointer->zwp_locked_pointer_v1)
     {
         zwp_locked_pointer_v1_set_cursor_position_hint(
                 pointer->zwp_locked_pointer_v1,
